N5008 [over.match.copy]/1.1, [class.conv.ctor]/2: in copy-initialization
`E e = 1;' only converting (non-explicit) constructors are candidates, so
the program is ill-formed.  The front end accepted it (bin53): it ran
constructor overload resolution over all constructors.  It now rejects a
copy-initialization from another type whose only viable one-argument
constructors are explicit.  After class template argument deduction the
same check rejects it, but by dropping the body
(cpp17_ctad_copy_initialization_explicit_constructor, KNOWNBUG).
test_converting.desc: the converting constructors are still selected.  g++
13 and clang++ 18 reject this program.
